comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T20:05:14.463Z",codex-agent,"Verified real SDK Task call items, parent/depth graph equality, idempotent result comments, closure and claim release through the SIGKILL and replay suites. Standalone library writes use native schema-field options with public SDK registration, not direct item files."
  "2026-10-18T21:34:24.874Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 extends terminal ledger evidence: failed child calls persist a typed failure code, append an idempotent RLM refusal comment, update usage, close and release. Resume reconciles terminal result and refusal evidence before returning a completed root. Root interruptions and untyped child interruptions remain resumable; completed roots with legacy unterminated children fail closed."
  "2026-10-18T23:30:58.684Z",codex-agent,"Review threads WKg and WKi: privacy checks test raw and JSON-escaped workspace, platform-separated ancestor and active credential needles. Loaded checkpoints validate complete settings, scope, snapshot ids, calls, fragment slices, steps, response usage and optional outcomes before casting. Corrupt null/scalar calls, missing steps, malformed slices and unsafe transport settings produce incomplete refusals for resume and replay; no transport inference occurs. Checkpoint settings reuse the same validator as normal reads."
  "2026-10-18T23:31:50.720Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: bypassing the decoded.calls validation loop makes the malformed-checkpoint regression fail with a non-incomplete error; removing validateRlmSettings from load makes unsafe checkpoint settings regressions fail. Removing escaped privacy matching makes the quoted/backslash/control-character secret regression fail. All three reverted functions restored byte-for-byte; complete proof runner passed 16/16."
